+So, matched on disturbance, **the entire count-robustness cost trend (0.733 / 0.824 / 0.941) is consistent with
+churn volume; the data do not support a band-size residual once churn is held.** This is the bigger finding and
+is reported first, per the ITEM-A rule. The 10-15↔30-40 gap closes exactly at both levels (0.775 vs 0.774,
+p=0.99) — clean.
