+### A-INDEP — churn-SENSITIVITY of robustness differs sharply by band (independent of the stratification/cross-band verdict)
+This result stands whether or not the matched cross-band comparison survives — it is a within-band slope, not a
+cross-band contrast. Robustness falls with churn in EVERY band, but the slope is steeply band-dependent:
+- **80-100: nearly churn-insensitive** — 0.947 → 0.953 → 0.934 → 0.933 across churn [0.07 … 0.45] (range ~0.02).
+- **30-40: moderate** — 0.890 → 0.861 → 0.826 → 0.774 across [0.20 … 0.92] (range ~0.12).
+- **10-15: steep** — 0.775 → 0.735 → 0.686 across [0.62 … 2.20] (range ~0.09 over a narrower churn window; the
+  per-unit-churn slope is the steepest of the three).
+The larger band not only retains more root on average but its retention **degrades far less per unit of
+disturbance**. This is a scale-of-robustness-STABILITY finding that is independent of the A.6 cross-band verdict.
