+### R2 — property-zero cause: NOT zero vulnerabilities; it is a FEATURE-LEVEL NO-OP [zero-vuln hypothesis FALSIFIED]
+Zero-drift property events reproduced exactly: **14 / 330 / 130** (10-15/30-40/80-100). Tested in the pre-committed order:
+1. **"already at zero vulnerabilities" — FALSE.** `pre_n_vulns==0` accounts for **0/14, 0/330, 0/130**. Every
+   zero-drift property node HAD vulnerabilities (modal state vulns=1,services=1,running=1: 10/14, 245/330, 119/130;
+   range vulns 1–5). Zero of them were empty nodes.
+2. **"node not visible in the pool" — FALSE.** `touched_node_visible==True` for **100%** of both zero-drift and
+   nonzero-drift property events. The node is in the pooled embedding.
+3. **CAUSE: feature-level no-op.** `delta_h_v_norm==0` for **14/14, 330/330, 130/130** — the changed node's OWN
+   embedding did not move at all. So the property change altered a node property that is **not part of the GNN
+   node-feature encoding**; it fired on a real, visible, vulnerable node but produced no feature change, hence no
+   node-embedding change, hence exactly zero pooled drift. The zeros are inert *by encoding*, not by empty nodes.
